//
// A durable created with a BackOff ladder does NOT keep the AckWait it asked for:
// the server stores BackOff[0] in its place. So "give this consumer a server
// ladder" and "keep this consumer's AckWait" are the same knob, not two — which
// is what rules a server ladder out for a loop whose handler legitimately runs
