// isTransientSubscribeErr extends [nuts.IsTransientSubscribeErr] with the modern
// jetstream client's equivalents.
//
// The go-nuts predicate keys on the LEGACY nats.* error values, and the
// jetstream package defines its own distinct ones — jetstream.ErrStreamNotFound
// is a *jsError carrying an APIError, not nats.ErrStreamNotFound — so
// errors.Is finds neither across the two. A consumer migrated to the modern
// client (COR-1254) would therefore have every rollout-ordering failure
// classified as a FAULT and logged at error, which is precisely the alert-eroding
// noise this package exists to prevent (COR-1228).
//
// ErrConsumerNotFound is transient here because on this path it is a race, not a
// verdict: a supervised runner recreates a durable that has gone missing, so the
// honest reading is "not there yet" for as long as the escalation window allows
// and a fault only once it has not come back.
//
// This belongs in go-nuts beside the predicate it extends; kept here until the
// modern-client migration has more than one adopter to generalise from.
func isTransientSubscribeErr(err error) bool {
	return nuts.IsTransientSubscribeErr(err) ||
		errors.Is(err, jetstream.ErrConsumerNotFound) ||
		errors.Is(err, jetstream.ErrConsumerNotActive) ||
		errors.Is(err, jetstream.ErrNoHeartbeat)
}

